        "original_id": "a937a6b1-f8df-507c-a00e-a9d9b7a7f19f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kingdom of Slavonia, Slavonian Military Frontier, Military Frontier\n- Organizations: Habsburg Monarchy, Austrian Empire, Austro-Hungarian Empire, Jesuits\n- People: Tomo Zdelarić\n\nFacts:\n- Tomo Zdelarić, born around 1531 and died on 8 April 1572, was the earliest Jesuit from the Habsburg Kingdom of Slavonia.\n- The Kingdom of Slavonia was a province of the Habsburg Monarchy and later the Austrian Empire from 1699 to 1868.\n- The southern parts of the regions of the Kingdom of Slavonia belonged to the Slavonian Military Frontier.\n- The Slavonian Military Frontier was a section of the Military Frontier.\n- The Military Frontier was a province along the southern borderland of the Habsburg Monarchy and later of the Austrian Empire and Austro-Hungarian Empire.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9818c1c3-93f7-51aa-972b-6e784274dc8b",
        "text": "Page: Kingdom of Slavonia. Sentence: The Kingdom of Slavonia (Croatian: \"Kraljevina Slavonija\" ; German: \"Königreich Slawonien\" ; Latin: \"Regnum Sclavoniae\" ; Hungarian: \"Szlavón Királyság\" ) was a province of the Habsburg Monarchy and the Austrian Empire that existed from 1699 to 1868.\nPage: Kingdom of Slavonia. Sentence: The southern parts of these regions were part of the Slavonian Military Frontier, which was a section of the Military Frontier.\nPage: Military Frontier. Sentence: The Military Frontier was a province straddling the southern borderland of the Habsburg Monarchy and later the Austrian and Austro-Hungarian Empire.\nPage: Tomo Zdelarić. Sentence: Tomo Zdelarić () (c. 1531 – 8 April 1572} was the earliest Jesuit from Habsburg Kingdom of Slavonia.",
